\b Middletons POS - Comprehensive User Guide\b0\par
\par
This guide covers all features in the system. Use it as a reference for daily operations, manager tasks, and developer tools.\par
\par
\b Navigation and Basics\b0\par
{\pard\li360
\bullet\tab Top navigation: POS, Receipts, Reports, and the hamburger menu (Configuration).\par
\bullet\tab Configuration menu: Manage Vendors, Manage Cashiers, Schedule, Gift Cards, Opening / Closing, Settings, and Close App.\par
\bullet\tab The app warns before leaving POS if a cart has items to prevent accidental loss.\par
\pard}
\par
\b POS (Sales)\b0\par
{\pard\li360
\bullet\tab Start a sale: choose Cashier and Payment at the top.\par
\bullet\tab Optional toggles: Back-date sale (choose Sale Date), No Tax (Tax Exempt) opens a modal to enter purchaser/organization and tax ID, Split tender allows two payment types.\par
\bullet\tab Add an item: enter Item name, Price, Qty (use the picker or type), Vendor name or code (auto-suggest), optional Discount (percent or amount) and Reason, and optional Comment. Click Add Item.\par
\bullet\tab Edit or remove items from the Cart list.\par
\bullet\tab Totals: Subtotal, Tax, Card fee on gift card sales, and Total update automatically.\par
\bullet\tab Cash payments: enter Cash Received to see Change Due.\par
\bullet\tab Gift card payments: enter card number and redeem amount; balance appears.\par
\bullet\tab Split tender: choose second tender and amount.\par
\bullet\tab Sell Gift Card: use the Sell Gift Card button to add a gift card sale item. If cards are not loaded, open Gift Cards to add a book.\par
\bullet\tab New Sale opens another sale tab; Cancel Sale clears the active sale.\par
\bullet\tab Print & Save: records the sale, plays the register sound, and opens the receipt for printing (or prints silently if enabled). The cart clears after printing.\par
\bullet\tab Gift card reminder: if the sale includes gift cards, a reminder prompts you to activate them on the Gift Cards page.\par
\pard}
\par
\b Receipts\b0\par
{\pard\li360
\bullet\tab Search and filter by receipt number, item, vendor, cashier, payment, date range, and void status.\par
\bullet\tab Vendor subtotals update to match the active filter.\par
\bullet\tab Actions: View opens a receipt, Print prints again.\par
\bullet\tab Void a receipt: choose cashier, enter a reason, and confirm. Voided receipts remain visible and are marked.\par
\bullet\tab Record returns: search a receipt, choose full return or selected items, add a reason, and update. Returns are marked on receipts.\par
\pard}
\par
\b Reports\b0\par
{\pard\li360
\bullet\tab Sales per Vendor: filter by date and vendor, run report, export CSV, or print summary/detailed reports.\par
\bullet\tab Credit card fee summary shows 5 percent of gross card sales per vendor.\par
\bullet\tab Tax Exempt Sales report is available in Manager Mode and includes purchaser info, receipt, totals, and cashier.\par
\bullet\tab Developer Mode shows Backup Data and Restore Data for full data backups.\par
\pard}
\par
\b Gift Cards\b0\par
{\pard\li360
\bullet\tab Book Intake: add a book using prefix, pad length, and start/end numbers to create cards.\par
\bullet\tab Activate cards from the Available list with amount, cashier, receipt (optional), and note.\par
\bullet\tab Lookup Balance: enter a card number to see balance and history.\par
\bullet\tab Inventory Summary: view available, active, and redeemed counts plus book summary.\par
\bullet\tab Lists: Available, Active (with balance), and Redeemed (receipt/date/amount/remaining).\par
\pard}
\par
\b Opening / Closing (Cash Drawer)\b0\par
{\pard\li360
\bullet\tab Opening: enter counts for each denomination and submit. Add a note if prompted for changes.\par
\bullet\tab Closing: enter closing counts, see the deposit amount, and submit the closing.\par
\bullet\tab Verify Deposit: confirm deposit total and enter a deposit number.\par
\bullet\tab Submit Daily Totals: review closing totals, deposit amount, and notes, then verify and submit.\par
\bullet\tab Print Deposit Report: enabled after closing data exists.\par
\bullet\tab Manager Mode unlocks drawer history and target comparisons.\par
\pard}
\par
\b Schedule\b0\par
{\pard\li360
\bullet\tab Week View shows daily shifts and assignments; use Prev/Next Week to navigate.\par
\bullet\tab Monthly Coverage provides a calendar view and print option.\par
\bullet\tab Configure Hours: set base shifts, store hours, and special hours for holidays or exceptions.\par
\pard}
\par
\b Vendors\b0\par
{\pard\li360
\bullet\tab Add vendor name and optional code. Codes speed POS entry and print on receipts.\par
\bullet\tab Edit or delete vendors as needed.\par
\pard}
\par
\b Cashiers\b0\par
{\pard\li360
\bullet\tab Add cashier names for POS selection and schedule assignment.\par
\bullet\tab Edit or remove names as needed.\par
\pard}
\par
\b Settings\b0\par
{\pard\li360
\bullet\tab Manager Mode unlocks sales tax, gift card surcharge, denomination targets, discount reasons, and vendor promotions.\par
\bullet\tab Sales Tax: set the percent rate used at POS.\par
\bullet\tab Gift Card Surcharge: applied to gift card sales paid by card.\par
\bullet\tab Denomination Targets: set expected drawer counts and target total.\par
\bullet\tab Discount Reasons: manage the POS discount reason list.\par
\bullet\tab Vendor Promotions: set vendor discounts with dates.\par
\bullet\tab Developer Mode toggles developer-only tools on other pages.\par
\bullet\tab Passwords: change manager/developer passwords.\par
\bullet\tab Printing: enable silent print, choose printer, and force greyscale receipts.\par
\bullet\tab Branding: set business name, address, phone, and receipt/report logo.\par
\bullet\tab App Version is shown at the bottom.\par
\pard}
\par
\b Closing the App\b0\par
{\pard\li360
\bullet\tab Use Configuration > Close App to exit safely. The app performs automatic backup on close.\par
\pard}
\par
\b Troubleshooting and Tips\b0\par
{\pard\li360
\bullet\tab If printing fails, check printer selection in Settings and retry Print & Save.\par
\bullet\tab For tax exempt sales, ensure purchaser name and tax ID are entered when No Tax is selected.\par
\bullet\tab Use manual backups regularly if you need copies outside the automatic backup folder.\par
\bullet\tab If data looks wrong, stop and consult a manager before restoring a backup.\par
\pard}
}
